L,lh4="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",lh$=[0,m],lia=[0,jt],lic=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],lid=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],lie=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],lif=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],lig=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],lih=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],lii=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],lij=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],lik=[0,"- **keybinding** \xe2\x80\x94 Key-capture editor for a string literal holding a keyboard shortcut; records the next chord pressed and commits it as the literal."],lil=[0,"- **color** \xe2\x80\x94 Color picker for an `Oklch(l, c, h)` literal: a swatch plus lightness, chroma and hue sliders. Attaches only to that constructor applied to three float literals."],lim=[0,0,0],lin=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],lio=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],liq=[0,m,0],lir=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],lis=iF(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),lit=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],liz=[0,m],liy="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",lix="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",liw="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",liu="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",liH=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],liG=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],liI=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],liE=[0,"Empty hole"],liD=hw,liC=[0,"Missing operator"],liA=[0,0,1],liB=[0,0,0],liJ=[0,[0,lh,[0,S,[0,[0,bP,[0,i,jL]],[0,[0,ks,[0,S,[0,[0,lP,[0,S,[0,o0A,o0z]]],0]]],[0,[0,hV,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lP],0]]],0]]]]],0],liK=dY,liL=[0,cx,[0,i,bsy]],liM=eQ,liN=[0,bP,[0,i,eQ]],liO=[0,[0,lh,[0,S,[0,[0,bP,[0,i,jL]],[0,[0,ks,[0,S,[0,[0,lP,[0,S,[0,o0C,o0B]]],0]]],[0,[0,hV,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lP],0]]],0]]]]],0],liP=dY,liQ=[0,cx,[0,i,bpR]],liR=eQ,liS=[0,bP,[0,i,eQ]],liT=[0,[0,lh,[0,S,[0,[0,bP,[0,i,jL]],[0,[0,ks,[0,S,[0,[0,lP,[0,S,[0,o0E,o0D]]],0]]],[0,[0,hV,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lP],0]]],0]]]]],0],liU=dY,liV=[0,cx,[0,i,bn9]],liW=eQ,liX=[0,bP,[0,i,eQ]],li$=[0,1],li8=[0,M$],li9=[0,da],li_=eL,li6=[0,40],li5=[0,Ks],li7=m,li4=[0,0],li1=[0,jt],li2=da,li3=eL,liY=bq3,liZ=dTZ,li0=b7G,lja=[0,0],lje=[0,0],ljg=[0,1],ljf=[0,m],ljK="Warning: using backup text! Serialization may be for an older version of Hazel.",ljI="persistence load",ljJ="PARSE FAILED (persistence load): loading empty buffer",ljF=[0,1],ljG=[0,0],ljH=[0,0],ljD=eL,ljE=bmt,ljB=eL,ljC=dFt,ljh=[0,[18,[1,[0,[11,d,0],d]],[11,aX,0]],aZ],lji=ua,ljj=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,x,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],y],ljk=[0,[3,0,0],aA],ljl=[0,[17,0,0],v],ljm=[0,[12,59,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]],B],ljn=akx,ljo=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,x,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],y],ljp=[0,[3,0,0],aA],ljq=[0,[17,0,0],v],ljr=[0,[17,[0,a,1,0],[12,az,[17,0,0]]],a0],ljz=akx,ljA=ua,ljx=akx,ljy=ua,ljv=[0,akx],ljw=[0,ua],l